{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1225"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/instruments","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__instruments.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",574],["-","logic."],["+","logic, and so does its big brother, the Contrabassoon. Sounding an octave below the bassoon, it is the lowest and largest woodwind instrument of the orchestra: its air column is almost six metres long and is folded back on itself three or four times. Michael Praetorius described early attempts at such an instrument in 1619; Beethoven used it in his Fifth and Ninth Symphonies, and Haydn lets it growl beneath the lion's roar in \"The Creation\"."],["=",456]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",520],["-","Logik."],["+","Logik, ebenso sein großer Bruder, das Kontrafagott. Es klingt eine Oktave tiefer als das Fagott und ist das tiefste und größte Holzblasinstrument des Orchesters: Seine Luftsäule ist fast sechs Meter lang und drei- bis viermal geknickt. Michael Praetorius beschrieb 1619 erste Versuche mit einem solchen Instrument; Beethoven setzte es in seiner Fünften und Neunten Sinfonie ein, und Haydn lässt es in der „Schöpfung“ unter dem Brüllen des Löwen grollen."],["=",436]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1225"},"reason":"a1225 body: lowercase \"the Woodwinds/The Flute/The Oboe/The Clarinet/the Contrabassoon\"; sentences reworded so they name the oboe (tuning A), the clarinet (Denner), the contrabassoon (lowest and largest) and the Querflöte (DE) explicitly; DE \"auf ein Mundstück geschraubt\" → \"mit einer Blattschraube am Mundstück befestigt\"","by":"enrich batch 127","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0589-a1585.md"},
